Read the relevant three cases in `raw/expanded-oracle-characterization.json` (SHA-256 `c54cfd826fff469ffb1f7005511a6b32ed8aff99a37ce7afc7b957d67dc93acf`), plus the installed oracle's `Result.__iter__`, `ResultRow.__new__`, and `FrozenBindings.__getitem__`/`project` implementations. The `sparql.py` source hash matches the new receipt: `938b13a453cf85f42b559bbf303c06d9710801fbc39dfcb87ff79fb87b15a55f`. The separately inspected `query.py` hash is `4423d11e10a43df7ee8fcb07d3c0918efd54cd5356e7f1808c8f3c5b98fa9d5f`. These are read-only inspections and root-executed oracle receipts, not a fresh test run by this reviewer.

| New witness | Exact planned observation | Source/evidence assessment |
|---|---|---|
| `empty-explicit-group` | Query with absent predicate and explicit GROUP BY, initial this=a, has public columns n/this and zero iterated rows | Receipt agrees; do not expose a padded internal empty mapping as a public result |
| `empty-subselect-init-fallback` | Outer SELECT this over an absent projected subquery and BIND fallback has zero iterated rows despite initial this=a | Receipt agrees; I fallback must not turn an empty projected actual domain into a visible row |
| `bind-bound-check` | Projected bound/this has one row containing typed boolean true and IRI a | Receipt agrees; a retained nonempty mapping may expose I fallback for a missing visible cell |

The oracle iteration checks `if b` before constructing ResultRow; ResultRow then calls `values.get` for public columns. FrozenBindings projection preserves only actual items, while its lookup can fall back to initial bindings. The added law correctly separates these steps and limits empty-mapping suppression to public SELECT presentation. It explicitly retains internal empty mappings for enclosing algebra, avoiding a premature filter inside subqueries or aggregate execution. It also leaves ASK/template/describe behavior tied to their separately witnessed laws.

No new unfalsifiable criterion, pre-emptive descope, unmapped requirement or planned-by-refusal was introduced. The new row names the actual compatibility Graph.query iteration entry point, exact receipt inputs and specific zero-row/true-a observations and maps them to Tasks 1/2. It strengthens the existing result/domain obligation; it does not count empty output as success for arbitrary reassignment inputs. No design or repository-constraint revision is required. No scope decision or `REWRITE TO` replacement is needed.

Implementation and native/shim parity remain unproved. Required next work is the existing complete compiler and consumer tasks with the new public-domain witnesses included. No source, environment, test, build or forge mutation occurred in this recheck; this appended report is the sole authored artifact.

